es_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/deployments","created_at":"2012-12-07T13:30:23Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T11:48:01Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-11T20:11:30Z","git_url":"git://github.com/python/mypy.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:python/mypy.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy","homepage":"https://www.mypy-lang.org/","size":77161,"stargazers_count":20064,"watchers_count":20064,"language":"Python","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":3065,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":3124,"license":{"key":"other","name":"Other","spdx_id":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["linter","python","typechecker","types","typing"],"visibility":"public","forks":3065,"open_issues":3124,"watchers":20064,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"body":"Please provide more information to help us understand the issue:\r\n\r\n* *Problem*\r\n  * I am using code to access module level variables through an alternative [reference created on import time following this recipe](https://stackoverflow.com/a/35904211/2889970). `mypy` reports an error on this, which I believe may be unnecessary.\r\n* *Are you reporting a bug, or opening a feature request?*\r\n  * Bug\r\n* *Please insert below the code you are checking with mypy, or a mock-up repro if the source is private. We would appreciate if you try to simplify your case to a minimal repro.*\r\n```python\r\n# a.py\r\nimport sys\r\nthis = sys.modules[__name__]\r\nthis.serializable_classes = {}  # a.py:15: error: Module has no attribute \"serializable_classes\"\r\nsetattr(this, \"serializable_classes\", {})  # alternative without mypy error\r\n```\r\n* *What is the actual behavior/output?*\r\n  * `error: Module has no attribute \"serializable_classes\"`\r\n* *What is the behavior/output you expect?*\r\n  * No error. It seems `mypy` applies rules for accessing a name from a module, while it really is an assignment. Why would the previous presence of a variable name in a module namespace matter under these circumstances?\r\n* *What are the versions of mypy and Python you are using?*\r\n```\r\n$ tox -e mypy\r\nmypy installed: mypackage==0.0.1,mypy==0.711,mypy-extensions==0.4.1,typed-ast==1.4.0\r\nmypy run-test-pre: PYTHONHASHSEED='349'\r\nmypy run-test: commands[0] | python --version\r\nPython 3.7.3\r\n```\r\n* *What are the mypy flags you are using? (For example --strict-optional)*\r\n```\r\n# mypy.ini\r\n[mypy]\r\nwarn_return_any = True\r\nwarn_unused_configs = True\r\n# and some import ignores below\r\n```\r\n* *Possibly relates issues*\r\n  * #1778","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/7171/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/7171/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]